IMPORT prelude
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g5-inspectors`
IMPORT `g5-test-conduct`

-- g5-tests-entry.l4: trap T30, the same place entered by an inspector (s.31(3)) and by a tester or expert (s.37).
-- Expected values were decided from the Hebrew of s.31(3) (inputs/law.wiki line 259) and s.37(a)(1) and (b) (lines
-- 308 and 313 to 317) BEFORE this was run.  The two sections differ: an inspector may enter a place that is not a
-- dwelling freely, and a dwelling on a court order OR the holder's consent, which has no form; a tester or expert
-- needs the holder's WRITTEN consent after an explanation, shows his instrument, and for a dwelling enters only at
-- the holder's request by prior arrangement; there is no court-order route for him.

§ `Tests of trap T30: entry by an inspector and by a tester or expert`

§§ `Fixtures`

`an inspector who is fully equipped` MEANS
    `An inspector at work` OF TRUE, (LIST `enter a place to supervise`), TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

`a tester doing an auxiliary test` MEANS
    `Tester or expert at work` OF `acting as a tester`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE

-- The place, as the inspector sees it: reason limb 1, reason limb 2, dwelling, court order, holder consented
--                                                        limb 1  limb 2  dwelling  order  consent
`a workshop, suspicion, no consent or order` MEANS `Place an inspector means to enter` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a dwelling, a court order, no consent`      MEANS `Place an inspector means to enter` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE
`a dwelling, consent of some kind, no order` MEANS `Place an inspector means to enter` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE
`a dwelling, neither`                        MEANS `Place an inspector means to enter` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE

-- The same places, as a tester or expert sees them: the senior inspector's reason (2 limbs); showed the instrument; written consent;
-- told the purpose; told the right to refuse; told the right to withdraw; told before consenting; withdrew; dwelling; asked; arranged
--                                                                        limb1 limb2 showed consent purpose refuse withdraw before withdrew dwelling asked arranged
`the workshop, no consent given`                  MEANS `Entry by a tester or an expert under section 37` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`the workshop, written consent after an explanation` MEANS `Entry by a tester or an expert under section 37` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`the dwelling, no consent given, court order exists` MEANS `Entry by a tester or an expert under section 37` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
`the dwelling, consent given orally only`         MEANS `Entry by a tester or an expert under section 37` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE
`the dwelling, written consent but the holder never asked` MEANS `Entry by a tester or an expert under section 37` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`the dwelling, everything the tester needs`       MEANS `Entry by a tester or an expert under section 37` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE

§§ `T30 -- the two entries side by side`

-- A place that is not a dwelling: the inspector needs no consent and no order; the tester or expert needs
-- the holder's written consent after an explanation.
#ASSERT `s 31(3) — the inspector may enter the place` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a workshop, suspicion, no consent or order`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(a)(1) — the tester or expert may enter the place` `a tester doing an auxiliary test` `the workshop, no consent given`
#ASSERT `s 37(a)(1) — the tester or expert may enter the place` `a tester doing an auxiliary test` `the workshop, written consent after an explanation`

-- A dwelling with a court order: the inspector may enter; for a tester or expert there is no court-order route.
#ASSERT `s 31(3) — the inspector may enter the place` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a dwelling, a court order, no consent`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(a)(1) — the tester or expert may enter the place` `a tester doing an auxiliary test` `the dwelling, no consent given, court order exists`

-- A dwelling with the holder's consent in no particular form: the inspector may enter; a tester or expert needs it
-- in writing, and the holder's own request and a prior arrangement besides.
#ASSERT `s 31(3) — the inspector may enter the place` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a dwelling, consent of some kind, no order`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(a)(1) — the tester or expert may enter the place` `a tester doing an auxiliary test` `the dwelling, consent given orally only`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(a)(1) — the tester or expert may enter the place` `a tester doing an auxiliary test` `the dwelling, written consent but the holder never asked`
#ASSERT `s 37(a)(1) — the tester or expert may enter the place` `a tester doing an auxiliary test` `the dwelling, everything the tester needs`

-- A dwelling with neither: neither may enter.
#ASSERT NOT `s 31(3) — the inspector may enter the place` `an inspector who is fully equipped` `a dwelling, neither`
